<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net9.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Authors>Alexandre G.P Cardoso</Authors>
    <Version>1.0.1</Version>
    <Description>Easily create and parse fixed-width strings for flat-file integrations, including CNAB files and mainframe systems, without manually handling substrings and padding.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/agpcardoso/AGPC.FixedLayout</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/agpcardoso/AGPC.FixedLayout</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>GIT</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>fixed-width fixed-length fixed-layout fixed-format flat-file flatfiles mainframe legacy-integration record-layout text-record CNAB files Fixed-Layout cnab-files</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Version 1.0.1 adds a native net9.0 target while retaining netstandard2.0 for existing consumers. No public API signatures have changed.

- Performance: Layout metadata is cached by DTO type, and serialization writes directly to a StringBuilder, reducing repeated reflection and temporary string allocations.
- Null collections: During ToConcatString(), a null collection marked with [FieldObjType] is treated as empty. A null single-object property still throws an exception to prevent subsequent fields from shifting.
- Thread-safe metadata cache: The metadata cache supports concurrent access. DTO instances should not be modified while they are being serialized.

See the README on GitHub for benchmark details: https://github.com/agpcardoso/AGPC.FixedLayout#version-101--whats-new</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\LICENSE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
